# /demo is this same app, built a second time in demo mode (real UI, an
# in-memory dataset instead of the real backend — see utils/demoMode.ts
# and build-with-demo.sh) and merged into this same static site's own
# dist/demo/ at build time. /demo/ (with the
# trailing slash) already serves dist/demo/index.html correctly via plain
# static-file-server directory-index behavior — no rule needed for that.
# The one real gap is the bare /demo (no trailing slash): confirmed live
# that an internal 200-rewrite rule for that exact path doesn't take
# effect (it falls through to the catch-all below instead, serving the
# main app), so this sends it as a real, visible 301 redirect to /demo/
# instead, which then hits the already-working case. Must come before the
# catch-all (rules match top-to-bottom, first match wins).
/demo /demo/ 301
/* /index.html 200
